<ol class="breathe-horizontal" start="1"> 


  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03772">arXiv:2611.03772</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.03772">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2611.03772">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2611.03772">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
      </p>
      <div class="tags is-inline-block">
        <span class="tag is-small is-link tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Cryptography and Security">cs.CR</span>
        
          
            <span class="tag is-small is-grey tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Artificial Intelligence">cs.AI</span>
          
        </div>
      
    </div>
    
    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        RuntimeTickets: Source-Grounded Security Obligations for <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Skills
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Gao%2C+K">Kuiyi Gao</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liu%2C+X">Xue Liu</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=He%2C+B">Bowei He</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2611.03772v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Third-party <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Skills extend what an autonomous&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2611.03772v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2611.03772v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2611.03772v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Third-party <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span> Skills extend what an autonomous <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> can do, but a malicious Skill can hide data exposure or output <span class="search-hit mathjax">manipulation</span> inside a legitimate workflow. Neither reading a Skill&#39;s description nor granting it tool permissions tells whether its execution meets the user&#39;s security requirements. We introduce RuntimeTickets, a protocol that enforces and audits these requirements while a Skill runs. From released malicious-Skill datasets we derive a risk model and build adversarial-benign Skill pairs. From the task&#39;s delivery contract, a language model proposes security obligations for that task. Each obligation cites the Skill lines it answers, and the ticket tightens the host&#39;s <span class="search-hit mathjax">approvals</span> into fine-grained allowed actions but never loosens them. A runtime gate checks the recipient, object and amount of every outbound send before forwarding it, and trusted monitors record the effects within their observation scope. The ticket links these checks and observations to the <span class="search-hit mathjax">approved</span> obligations of each Skill run, and a deterministic decoder turns the ticket&#39;s status into governable data flows and verifies each obligation. Neither enforcement nor decoding involves a language model, so text injected by a Skill can change the proposal but never the rule that decides a send. We evaluate RuntimeTickets at the network egress boundary of three unmodified <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> frameworks against production Skill scanners and runtime baselines, among them an AgentBound-derived allow-list and SkillGuard. RuntimeTickets eliminated both failure modes of current Skill defenses, overlook (malicious Skills let through) and overkill (benign Skills blocked): its overlook rate was 0.0% and its overkill rate 0.0%, while the scanners erred on both sides. RuntimeTickets ties <span class="search-hit mathjax">approved</span> requirements to verifiable execution evidence and offers a common foundation for the safe and auditable deployment of third-party Skills.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2611.03772v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2611.03772v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 2 November, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> November 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">27 Pages, Submitted to ICLR 2027 (Under review)</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
  </li>

  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.33446">arXiv:2610.33446</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.33446">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2610.33446">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2610.33446">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
      </p>
      <div class="tags is-inline-block">
        <span class="tag is-small is-link tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Robotics">cs.RO</span>
        </div>
      
    </div>
    
    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        MOTIO: <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agentic</span> Skill Engineering for Reality-Grounded Humanoid Loco-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Manipulation</span>
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=SpatialtemporalAI"> SpatialtemporalAI</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.33446v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        We present MOTIO, an <span class="search-hit mathjax">agentic</span> skill-engineering system that turns ordinary human-action videos, reality-grounded 3D assets, motion references, and reusable robot skills into executable humanoid loco-&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.33446v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2610.33446v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2610.33446v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        We present MOTIO, an <span class="search-hit mathjax">agentic</span> skill-engineering system that turns ordinary human-action videos, reality-grounded 3D assets, motion references, and reusable robot skills into executable humanoid loco-<span class="search-hit mathjax">manipulation</span> programs. Through in-context task and contact reasoning, an <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span> constructs staged robot-native interactions and improves them using physics execution, multi-frame feedback, and human validation---without task-specific teleoperation or robot demonstration collection. <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agentic</span> 3D supplies metric product and environment assets, while existing whole-body, inverse-kinematics, and dexterous-hand interfaces realize the programs. Across 33 timestamped first <span class="search-hit mathjax">approvals</span>, the median recorded <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span>-turn time is 97.0 minutes and request-to-<span class="search-hit mathjax">approval</span> duration is 2.80 hours. Simulation-side layout and object variation prepare a long-horizon bottle-disposal skill for a continuous 101.75-second physical G1 execution in a scanned office; physical refinement reduces screw-tightening thread residual by 76.0%. <span class="search-hit mathjax">Agent</span>-generated skills additionally supervise BC/DAgger distillation into one shared reference policy, completing 18 simulated tasks under the same checkpoint without inference-time expert intervention.
Project page: https://iiiiqiiii.github.io/motio/
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2610.33446v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2610.33446v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 24 October, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> October 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">24 pages, including 11 pages of supplementary material</span>
    </p>
    

    

    
  </li>

  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.23859">arXiv:2609.23859</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.23859">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2609.23859">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2609.23859">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
      </p>
      <div class="tags is-inline-block">
        <span class="tag is-small is-link tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Human-Computer Interaction">cs.HC</span>
        </div>
      
    </div>
    
    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Vibe-GUIDE: A Graph-based User Interface in IDEs for Oversight in Vibe Coding
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Chou%2C+C">Chifang Chou</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Lee%2C+S+Y">Sam Yu-Te Lee</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Choudhuri%2C+R">Rudrajit Choudhuri</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ma%2C+K">Kwan-Liu Ma</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2609.23859v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        In <span class="search-hit mathjax">agentic</span> coding, developers shift from implementing changes themselves to specifying intent, evaluating the&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2609.23859v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2609.23859v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2609.23859v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        In <span class="search-hit mathjax">agentic</span> coding, developers shift from implementing changes themselves to specifying intent, evaluating the <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent&#39;s</span> work, and making <span class="search-hit mathjax">approval</span> decisions. However, delegating implementation can introduce cognitive debt that erodes project comprehension over time, constraining developers&#39; ability to provide oversight. In this work, we investigate the role of persistent shared representations in supporting project comprehension and oversight of coding <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span>. We present Vibe-GUIDE, an <span class="search-hit mathjax">agentic</span> coding interface built around a structural, live, <span class="search-hit mathjax">manipulable</span>, and adaptive graph representation organized by functional modules. We evaluated our interface in a randomized between-subjects study comparing how 16 developers completed three cumulative coding tasks using our interface or a Chat-only baseline. We found that Vibe-GUIDE can support project comprehension and sustained task performance while keeping developers cognitively involved in oversight. These findings show how persistent shared representations can complement natural-language interaction and help developers maintain the understanding needed to oversee <span class="search-hit mathjax">agent</span>-generated changes as projects evolve.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2609.23859v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2609.23859v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 20 September, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> September 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">14 pages, 3 figures, 4 tables</span>
    </p>
    

    
      <p class="comments is-size-7">
        

        

        
          <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">ACM Class:</span>
